XPU: run block-FP8 checkpoints on the weight-only W8A16 kernel
(VLLM_XPU_FP8_BLOCK_TO_CHANNEL=1).

At load time, dequantize each block-scaled FP8 weight and requantize it to
per-output-channel FP8, then serve it with fp8_gemm_w8a16 (bf16 activations)
instead of dynamic-activation W8A8 fp8_gemm. On Arc Pro B70 the W8A16 kernel
is ~2x faster at every batch size (M=1..2048) and accuracy is equal (weight
requant error ~= the activation-quant error it replaces).

